<%#
  SMP-1853 — CZID-285 Layer 3 clearance UX. Shown when a user's denied-party screening has not come back
  clear: a hit or an error puts access on HOLD pending compliance review. This is NOT a denial — the hold
  is released by a compliance officer (the resolution poller auto-clears it), so it uses the amber "under
  review" treatment (matching the signup pending page), not the red deny treatment. Rendered with HTTP 403.

  "Check again" re-runs the clearance: it returns the same held result until the officer clears the hold,
  at which point it is the way back in. Sign out is the only other affordance.

  Approval model (legal-approved 2026-08-24): clearance is attestation + denied-party screening, with no
  identity-verification step, so the copy speaks only to screening.
%>
<%= render "export_control/styles" %>
<main class="ec-page">
  <div class="ec-card ec-card--pending">
    <p class="ec-pill">Under review</p>
    <h1 class="ec-h1">Access under review</h1>
    <div class="ec-body" role="status">
      <p>
        Access to export-controlled functions requires a clear denied-party screening. Your screening has
        not come back clear yet, so your access is on hold while it is reviewed. You will be able to continue
        once the review is complete.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ec-actions">
      <%= link_to "Check again", new_export_control_clearance_path, class: "ec-btn ec-btn--primary" %>
      <%= link_to "Sign out", auth0_logout_path, class: "ec-btn ec-btn--secondary" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
